64b2e25d is the commit of ../../cascade/SOURCE. Its bb.train trained S55, S55' and S55'-deep (their job files pin
the trees b142837ebd183cfcdfea419520d0429f9f2d5c8c and c69800c1dee46d02346076593819f066aafe4138, whose bb.train and
bb.cascade_train differ from 64b2e25d's only in the --family option the fitted runs added); its bb.cascade_train
trained C14, C6, C14' and C6'. The same bb.train, with every option added after a run off by default (its docstring),
runs the arguments of the earlier BB networks: r11, r12 and r21 (5c6edafcd91d1170d265df13599d23738793fb94 on
ising-bb), g2_A3D (5515f70914aef53ea7ec631687b57384f20d1a7a on ising-bb-gross2) and the gross trunk and its cooldown
(d71bc5633ee95a6ac668c1d999cc6d4d5a97a5e8 or a later commit of ising-bb-gross2); 5c6edafc, 5515f709 and d71bc563 are
ancestors of 64b2e25d. The gross stages were started by ising_compare/bb/gross2.py on ising-bb-gross2 (a pod driver,
not included); ../TRAINING.md gives their arguments, which the released network's own record confirms
for the last stage.

Not included: the Cascade re-implementation's notes that comments cite (bb/cascade/*.md), bb/checks.py and
bb/test_cascade.py (the training stage's tests), the Relay-BP circuits (qldpc_neural/scripts/fetch_relay.sh clones
them; qnd.circuits checks each file's sha256 against data/circuit_manifest.csv).
